  "body": "The maintainer reported this in chat on 2026-11-15. His words: \"bug; examples is not shippped with dist package.\"\n\n## What happens\n\nThe release packages do not contain the `examples/` directory. A user who installs CamCraft from a package has no example project to open.\n\nThe repository has these tracked files in `examples/`: `first-part.camproj`, `first-part.nc`, `first-router-part.camproj` and `models/`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe staged tree of the Windows zip and installer comes from one list, and `examples` is not in it:\n\n```rust\n// xtask/src/release_pack.rs:59\npub const ASSET_DIRS: &[&str] = &[\"assets/posts\", \"assets/machines\", \"assets/ui\", \"assets/scripts\", \"assets/themes\"];\n```\n\nThe other packages (TAR.GZ, DEB, RPM, AppImage, Snap, Flatpak, the macOS app, the FreeBSD tarball, AUR) have their own staging in `.github/workflows/release.yml` and in `scripts/`. They are not yet read for this issue.\n\n## For the work\n\n1. Add `examples/` to the staged tree of each package type. Read each packager and list the result for each in the PR.\n2. Check that each example project opens from the installed location. A `.camproj` that refers to its model by a relative path must find `models/` in the package.\n3. Decide where the examples are installed on each system (next to the executable, or a shared data directory) and how the user finds them (for example a File menu entry). Record the choice in `docs/decisions/`. A menu entry is a follow-up issue if it is not small.\n4. Add a check that fails when a package has no examples: a unit test on the stage list, and a `tar -tzf` / `unzip -l` line in `release.yml` next to the existing checks.\n\n`xtask/` is a process file: the PR body has the line `Process change: yes`. Do not add a workflow trigger.\n\n## Done means\n\n- The Windows zip and installer, and each Linux, macOS and FreeBSD package, contain the examples.\n- A test on the stage list pins `examples/first-part.camproj` and the `models/` files.\n- Each example project opens from the packaged layout with its model.\n",
